---
import Layout from "@roastbook/open-coffee-ui/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import { buildDate, version } from "../lib/data";
import "../styles/pages.css";
const UA = "RoastbookOpenCoffeeBot/1.0 (+https://data.roastbook.coffee/bot)";
---
<Layout title="Crawler" site="data" version={version} buildDate={buildDate} description="RoastbookOpenCoffeeBot: what it reads, how it behaves and how to opt out.">
  <Nav current="bot" />
  <h1>RoastbookOpenCoffeeBot</h1>
  <p class="lead">If you saw this user agent in your logs, it was us: the Sourcing agent of Roastbook Open Coffee, an open dataset of coffee places.</p>
  <pre><code>{UA}</code></pre>

  <h2>What it reads</h2>
  <p>A café's or roaster's own public pages: home, about, menu, shop and legal notice (Impressum). It extracts facts such as opening hours, whether filter coffee is served, which roasters are served and the operating company, and cites the page as the source.</p>
  <p>It never copies texts or photos, never logs in, and does not read Instagram posts or captions. Descriptions in the dataset are written from the extracted facts only.</p>

  <h2>How it behaves</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Respects <code>robots.txt</code>, including rules for <code>RoastbookOpenCoffeeBot</code> and <code>*</code>.</li>
    <li>At most one request per second per host, and only a handful of pages per site.</li>
    <li>Caches pages for 30 days; a full re-check runs about twice a year, opening hours and status quarterly.</li>
    <li>Runs from GitHub Actions on a schedule; every change goes through a public, reviewed pull request in <a href="https://github.com/Roastbook/open-coffee-data">Roastbook/open-coffee-data</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Opt out</h2>
  <p>Add this to your <code>robots.txt</code> and the crawler will not fetch your site again:</p>
  <pre><code>{`User-agent: RoastbookOpenCoffeeBot
Disallow: /`}</code></pre>
  <p>To have your place removed or corrected, <a href="https://github.com/Roastbook/open-coffee-data/issues/new/choose">open an issue</a> or email <a href="mailto:data@roastbook.coffee">data@roastbook.coffee</a>. Owners can also claim their place and submit facts and photos themselves; see <a href="https://github.com/Roastbook/open-coffee-data/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:data@roastbook.coffee">data@roastbook.coffee</a> · Roastbook, maintainers of Roastbook Open Coffee.</p>
</Layout>
